  "election_date": "2026-11-03",
  "description": "The 2026 election for Wisconsin's 1st Congressional District will determine who represents southeastern Wisconsin—including Racine, Kenosha, and Janesville—in the U.S. House. Incumbent Republican Rep. Bryan Steil, first elected in 2018, is seeking a fifth term and chairs the House Administration Committee. The district has been held by Republicans since 1994 and is rated as Likely Republican by The Cook Political Report, though a crowded Democratic primary field sees the seat as a potential flip opportunity. The Democratic primary on August 11, 2026, will determine who challenges Steil in the general election, with candidates emphasizing health care, affordability, and labor issues.",
